{"language_code":"eng","language_probability":0.9578455090522766,"text":"If you woke up tomorrow in a zombie apocalypse, the United States military already has a plan for it. It's 2011, and in a quiet strategic command office, a few junior officers are writing a real document called Counter-Zombie Dominance. Page by page, they sort the undead into types: radiation zombies, evil magic zombies, vegetarian zombies, which only eat plants, space zombies, which turn out to be dead satellites, only dangerous if they fall on you, and chicken zombies, which the plan calls the only kind proven to actually exist. That same spring, the CDC, the people who fight real epidemics, posts a zombie survival guide on its blog. Normally, a few thousand people read it. This time, so many show up, the website crashes. Luckily, the government was ready for zombies. Unluckily, its website wasn't ready for readers. You see, nobody thought the dead would rise. A made-up enemy let planners practice without any real country thinking the plan was about them. And the CDC's list? Water, food, a flashlight, medicine, a first aid kit. Ever packed for a camping trip? It's the same bag you'd need for a hurricane, a flood, or a blackout. The CDC liked the reaction so much it turned the guide into a comic book. So if you wake up and the street is full of zombies, don't panic. Grab the camping bag and keep an eye on the chickens.","words":[{"text":"If","start":0.08,"end":0.16,"type":"word","logprob":-0.000045536911784438416},{"text":" ","start":0.16,"end":0.2,"type":"spacing","logprob":-4.768370445162873e-7},{"text":"you","start":0.2,"end":0.26,"type":"word","logprob":-4.768370445162873e-7},{"text":" ","start":0.26,"end":0.3,"type":"spacing","logprob":-7.152555099310121e-7},{"text":"woke","start":0.3,"end":0.42,"type":"word","logprob":-7.152555099310121e-7},{"text":" ","start":0.42,"end":0.48,"type":"spacing","logprob":-3.576278118089249e-7},{"text":"up","start":0.48,"end":0.54,"type":"word","logprob":-3